mistral.rs PANICS generating from any Idefics3/SmolVLM model, because its
per-image encoder cache assumes a model that does NOT tile.

    mistralrs-core/src/vision_models/idefics3/mod.rs ~line 193

        let n = pixel_values.dim(0)?;                        // TILES
        let mut per_image: Vec<Option<Tensor>> = vec![None; n];
        ...
        for (i, &hash) in image_hashes.iter().enumerate() {  // IMAGES
            ...                                              // fills [0..n_images)
        }
        ...
        let slices: Vec<Tensor> = per_image.into_iter().map(|t| t.unwrap()).collect();
                                                                   ^^^^^^^^ panics

`per_image` is sized by the number of dim-0 slices in `pixel_values` and filled
by the number of images. For a model with dynamic-resolution tiling one image
becomes MANY slices — SmolVLM produces 17 (a 4x4 grid plus a global thumbnail)
for a single 512px input — so every slot from `n_images` to `n` stays `None`
and the `unwrap()` fires.

Observed: `HuggingFaceTB/SmolVLM-256M-Instruct` loads cleanly in 8.3 s and then

    thread '<unnamed>' panicked at idefics3/mod.rs:233:75:
    called `Option::unwrap()` on a `None` value

THE CRATE ALREADY KNOWS THIS INVARIANT
--------------------------------------
`mistralrs-core/src/paged_attention/encoder_cache.rs` has a shared helper,
`cached_encode_images`, documented as:

    Helper: cache-aware batch encoding for "Pattern A" models whose
    pixel_values have shape (N, C, H, W) with one image per dim-0 slice.

…and it sizes its `hits` vector by `image_hashes.len()` (correct) and carries

    debug_assert_eq!(n_images, pixel_values.dim(0)?,
                     "image_hashes length must match pixel_values dim-0");

Idefics3 open-codes that logic instead of calling the helper, inverts the
sizing, and drops the assertion. And because the assertion is a `debug_assert`,
it is COMPILED OUT of a release build — which is why the failure surfaces as a
bare `unwrap()` on `None` rather than as the message that names the cause.

SmolVLM is simply not a Pattern-A model. Tiling is the whole reason it reads
documents well, and it is what the FFai launch plan (§3.1.2) flags as
"load-bearing for document scores".

THE FIX
-------
Take the cache path only when the model actually IS one-image-per-slice, and
otherwise fall through to the existing uncached branch — which is already
correct, forwarding the whole tile batch in one call. Behaviour is unchanged
for non-tiling Idefics3 models; tiling models stop panicking and lose only a
cache they were never eligible for.

    -            let image_hidden_states = if !image_hashes.is_empty() {
    +            let image_hidden_states = if !image_hashes.is_empty()
    +                && image_hashes.len() == pixel_values.dim(0)?
    +            {

